ahoe, CO; Denver, CO; Douglas, CO; Jefferson, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.243371023415feaa4c3fe5781072da087af4c00f.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.243371023415feaa4c3fe5781072da087af4c00f.001.1"},{"event":"Special Weather Statement","headline":"Special Weather Statement issued August 15 at 1:16PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"At 116 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm over\nIndian Hills, or 18 miles southwest of Denver, moving east at 15 mph.\n\nHAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph and half inch size hail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around\nunsecured objects. Minor damage to outdoor objects is\npossible.\n\nLocations impacted include...\nLakewood, southern Golden, Evergreen, Morrison, Tiny Town, Red\nRocks Park, Indian Hills, Idledale, Kittredge, Aspen Park,\nChatfield Reservoir, Ken Caryl, Pleasant View, Genesee and\nColumbine.","ends":"2026-08-15T13:45:00-06:00","severity":"Moderate","areaDesc":"Jefferson and West Douglas Counties Above  6000 Feet/Gilpin/Clear Creek/Northeast Park Counties Below 9000 Feet; Boulder And Jefferson Counties Below 6000 Feet/West Broomfield County","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ad8f6e434908adc7b8eef9815375ae2585e7a942.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ad8f6e434908adc7b8eef9815375ae2585e7a942.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Advisory","headline":"Flood Advisory issued August 15 at 1:05PM MDT until August 15 at 4:00PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Southeastern Clear Creek County in central Colorado...\nWest Central Jefferson County in central Colorado...\nNorthern Park County in central Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 400 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n\n- At 105 PM MDT, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges\nindicated heavy rain due to thunderstorms. Minor flooding is\nongoing or expected to begin shortly in the advisory area.\nBetween 0.5 and 1 inch of rain has fallen.\n\n- Additional rainfall amounts up to 0.5 inches are expected over\nthe area. This additional rain will result in minor flooding.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nEvergreen, Brookvale, Aspen Park, Kittredge, Indian Hills, Tiny\nTown, Idledale, Wah Keeney Park and Genesee.","ends":"2026-08-15T16:00:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Clear Creek, CO; Jefferson, CO; Park, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e67973d082a3416931585c7ed9848f9a2784eb23.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e67973d082a3416931585c7ed9848f9a2784eb23.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-15T19:12:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 151912 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 112 PM MDT Sat Aug 15 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Another round of showers and thunderstorms this afternoon and evening. Heavy rainfall and flash flooding are the main threats today. A few thunderstorms could become severe, with strong winds and hail possible. - Monsoon moisture lasts through Sunday, brin","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-15T19:21:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Rest of today through Sunday... Moisture will remain high across the area today, as scattered to numerous showers and thunderstorms move through again this afternoon and evening. Heavy rainfall may lead to localized flash flooding, particularly for the areas that saw heavy rainfall over the last several days and burn scars. Minimum RHs will remain above 30% with below normal temperat","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"cht01","station_name":"Chatfield at South Platte Reservoir","distance_km":15.4,"soil_temp_5cm_f":